  "authoritative_interpretation_of_slashes": "Per WMO Manual on Codes (WMO-No. 306) and ICAO Annex 3 Section 4.6.5, /// in an automated AUTO METAR indicates that cloud type and/or cloud amount is unidentifiable by the automated optical ceilometer sensor. It does NOT signify BKN/OVC, 6 oktas, or 0 oktas by default. However, when accompanied by a height code (e.g. ///030///), the cloud base height is explicitly measured by the ceilometer (030 = 3000 ft = 914.4 m). Therefore, height is preserved as an observed ceilometer measurement (914.4 m), while cloud amount is treated as unknown/missing and causally imputed without inventing arbitrary okta values.",
